UK’s largest database of parental leave policies. Browse over 800 policies giving you transparency and data to negotiate more money for your parental leave.\n\n# What People Are Saying\n\n“Thank you for your account and website I was able to negotiate a better maternity leave package all down to your extensive research. Its a step up from the statutory currently on offer and will be such a big help for us.”\n\nHolly\n\n“You gave me the balls to negotiate my maternity pay and I’ve gone from SMP to full pay for 12 weeks and half pay for 33 weeks.”\n\nHannah\n\n“You were the reason I found out about the Alabaster Ruling and got a lump sum paid to me after I sent your advice to my HR.”\n\nAlice\n\n# The Membership\n\nThe #1 financial community for new parents.\n\nGiving you insight, support, transparency and community during the first few years of parenthood.\n\nMasterclasses\n\nChildcare for High Earners\n\n£19.99\n\nWhen: 17th November @ 7.30pm\n\nWhere: Zoom (if you can’t make the live we send you the recording!)\n\nIn this session, we are honing in on the finances for high earners once you are returning to work.\n\nIf you or your partner earn over 100k you lose access to government childcare schemes. With 30 funded hours coming into play this September in England, losing out on this childcare help will become more painful than ever.\n\n  * What are the rules around net adjusted income?\n\n  * How much should you sacrifice into your pension before it stops becoming worth it?\n\n  * Should you reject your pay rise or go part-time?\n\n  * Are workplace nursery schemes a silver bullet for high earners?\n\n  * How do you weigh up your options?\n\nWe’ve teamed up with Philly Ponniah, Chartered Wealth Manager and financial coach to deliver a session tailored to these concerns. We will also be looking at estate planning once you’ve had a baby, and how to set your child up for financial success.\n\nSuitable for those earning between £80,000 - £140,000 individually\n\nFunded childcare spoken about refers to England. You can use the same principles to become eligible for tax-free childcare, which is UK wide.\n\nWhat you will learn:\n\n  * What childcare schemes are available\n\n  * What to look out for when you earn around 100k re-funded hours and tax-free childcare\n\n  * How do you work out whether reducing your salary for childcare schemes is worth it?\n\n  * Should you go part time to access childcare benefits?\n\n  * Flexible working requests\n\nRead more →\n\nEverything You Need to Know Post Birth 2026\n\n£14.99\n\nWHEN: 21st October @ 7.30pm\n\nWHERE: On Zoom (the session will be recorded if you can’t make the live!)\n\nFor expecting parents and anyone in the first few months.\nOne evening, two experts: Becca from A Mother Place on physical recovery, pelvic floor and the emotional side, and Nugget on the money admin, including child benefit, checking your pension and managing on leave pay. This class includes all the things baby classes should teach you - but often don’t.\n\nWednesday 21 October, 7.30pm on Zoom · 60 mins + Q&A\nCan’t make it live? Everyone gets the recording.\n\nBecca (A Mother Place) will guide you through:\n\n  * Body After Baby: Real talk about the first poo, bleeding, \"mum tum,\" and more.\n\n  * Pelvic Floor Fitness: When and how to start those essential exercises.\n\n  * Emotional Well-being: Understanding night sweats, baby blues, and the importance of self-care.\n\n  * Bonding with Baby: Why it's not always instant and how to navigate those early days.\n\n  * Finding Your New Normal: Creating routines (or not!) that work for you and your family.\n\n  * Relationship Resilience: How to maintain a strong partnership through the transition to parenthood.\n\nNugget will guide you through:\n\n  * Managing your money after the baby\n\n  * Child benefit, when & how to register\n\n  * Protecting your and your children’s future\n\n  * Checking your pension is correct\n\nRead more →\n\nHow to Start Investing for your Children\n\n£24.99\n\nThe world of investing can seem murky and confusing, so we've teamed up with award-winning Family Wealth Manager Sophia Jarvis, founder of MIA (the UK's first female-led investment app), to deliver a straightforward session on how to get started.\nMost parents wish they'd started sooner. This is your chance to get ahead. In five steps, this session will teach you how to give your child a real financial head start:\n1. Laying the Foundations — Why an emergency fund comes before any investing decision, and how to build one\n2. Choosing the Right Child Accounts — Cash vs. investing, explained simply, so you can pick what's right for your family\n3. Making the Most of Tax-Efficient Incentives — The clever, often-missed ways to save on tax and bag government bonuses\n4. Getting Family & Friends Involved — How to steer generous relatives away from another pile of plastic toys and toward contributions that actually grow\n5. Staying on Track — How to set and hit real goals, whether that's university fees, a first house deposit, or even their retirement\nMeet your host: Sophia Jarvis\n\nSophia is an award-winning Family Wealth Manager who spotted a gap in the market and founded MIA - the UK's first female-led investment app, designed to help modern families and loved ones easily contribute towards children's future milestones like university, a first house deposit, and even retirement.\nAs a mum of twins, Sophia knows firsthand the worries parents face when navigating their child's future - particularly mums, a community underserved by financial services and one MIA is built to support. She's passionate about helping parents and loved ones give children a genuine financial head start, and her expertise has been featured in FemaleInvest, HELLO, The Times, and FT Adviser.\n\nRead more →\n\nHow do you afford baby number two?\n\n£19.99\n\n\"I don't think we can afford another baby.\"\n\nIf that thought has crossed your mind, you're not alone. 90% of the Nugget community told us the same thing: money is the main reason they're hesitating on baby number two.\n\nAnd it makes sense. You've likely just found your feet after a stretch of low income on maternity leave, childcare costs are already stretching things, and now you're weighing up doing it all again… maybe alongside a house move, remortgaging, or costs you didn't have first time round.\n\nBut \"can we afford it\" is rarely a yes-or-no question. It's a \"how\" question, and most people just haven't sat down and worked out the how yet.\n\nHaving a child is time-limited. Not knowing the numbers shouldn't be what decides it for you.\n\nSo, how do you actually afford baby number two? Join 165+ parents who've already done this masterclass!\n\nWe will be looking at:\n\n👉What maternity pay will you get a second time around?\n\n👉How to manage childcare costs on maternity leave\n\n👉 What you need to think about before going on your second maternity leave if you need a bigger house / to remortgage\n\n👉Avoiding the pension gap\n\n👉Why playing the just below £100k game will be even more important when you have baby no 2\n\n👉How to avoid the flexible working trap\n\n👉Is there a perfect age gap between children for your finances?\n\n✅ Recording available if you can’t make the live\n\n🙋🏻‍♀️ Time for your questions at the end\n\nRead more →\n\n# Bestselling Masterclasses\n\n# \n\n# \n\nOver 4000 happy customers since 2023.\n\nExplore the library\n\n# Start planning for your parental leave\n\nUse our comprehensive planners to accurately forecast your income over your maternity leave.\n\nFeatured\n\nThe Ultimate Parental Leave Money Planner\n\n£14.99\n\nParental leave is one of the biggest financial shifts you'll go through — and most couples plan it on the back of a napkin.\n\nThis planner does the opposite. It's the tool 900+ parents have used to get organised before leave starts: track both incomes, split shared costs fairly, hit your savings goal, and walk into leave knowing exactly where you stand… instead of finding out three months in.\n\n### What it actually does:\n\n  * Auto-calculates your key dates — due date, qualifying week, notice deadlines, earliest leave start, so you're not stressing about \"when do I tell my employer\" at 2am.\n\n  * Splits your finances properly. Separate tabs for Partner 1, Partner 2, and shared costs, so it's not just \"mum's spreadsheet\" — both of you can see where the money's coming from and going.\n\n  * Shows you the gap before it happens. The Overview tab compares your normal income to your leave income month by month and flags any shortfall in red, so you know exactly what you're saving for.\n\n  * Tracks your savings goal with live pie charts — set a target, log what you save, watch it fill in.\n\n  * Comes with a baby buy list built in, so the \"what do we actually need to buy\" spiral has a home.\n\n  * Video walkthroughs on every single tab. You're never staring at a blank spreadsheet wondering what goes where.\n\n(Note: this planner won't calculate your maternity/paternity pay amount for you — it's built to help you plan around it once you know the number. More on that below.)\n\nRead more →\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nNugget Savings | LinkedIn (https://www.linkedin.com/company/nugget-savings)\nciteturn83search6 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 weeks ago; \n\nImage: Nugget Savings’ cover photo\n\n# Nugget Savings\n\n## Technology, Information and Media\n\n  * Discover all 3 employees\n\n## About us\n\nWe are here to help you create a financially secure maternity leave. Giving you insight, support and community whilst planning your parental leave\n\nWebsite\n    https://www.nuggetsavings.com/\n\nIndustry\n    Technology, Information and Media\n\nCompany size\n    2-10 employees\n\nHeadquarters\n    London\n\nType\n    Privately Held\n\n## Locations\n\n  * Primary\n\nLondon, GB\n\n## Employees at Nugget Savings\n\n  * Clara Wilcox I Return To Work and Career Coach for Parents\n  * Harriet M.\n  * Katie Guild Katie Guild is an Influencer\nSee all employees\n\n## Updates\n\n  * Nugget Savings\n\n2,128 followers\n\n2mo\n\nLast time we ran one of these sessions I answered over 50 questions in 30 minutes and I’m not even joking 😅 If you’re looking for some clarity, support & advice on childcare for your baby - join this session! I’ll be covering every bit of support available in the UK including: 🙌 Tax-free childcare 🙌 Funded hours 🙌 Flying start scheme 🙌 Funded hours @ 2 🙌 Hiring a nanny 🙌 UC childcare 🙌 Workplace Nursery Benefit 🙌 Northern Ireland Childcare Subsidy Scheme Links in the comments! If you can’t make the live, buy a ticket and we’ll send you a recording the next day xxx\n\n[Button: …more ]\n\n`` `` ``\n\n  * Nugget Savings\n\n2,128 followers\n\n7mo\n\nP.S. To the brands following along: Our audience is incredible, but they are burnt out. Want to help me cheer them up with a Mother’s Day partnership? My DMs are open…let’s give these women the break they deserve. 🍸\n\nKatie Guild Katie Guild is an Influencer\n\n7mo Edited\n\nWhat do you want for mother’s day? Honestly? These answers make me a little sad. We asked the Nugget Savings community and they said: ❤️24hrs of doing zero childcare  ❤️To be fed and to not have to make a single thing all day  ❤️Full nights deep sleep 12 hours ❤️The day OFF. For real. No mental load for the day or week ahead ❤️A lie-in ❤️A pelvic floor specialist  ❤️ 4 hours entirely on my own  ❤️ My partner to say he’s proud of me ❤️ To be able to return to work part time post maternity leave ❤️ For no-one to touch me ❤️To not have to take unpaid leave to look after my sick toddler AGAIN ❤️ To feel appreciated  ❤️ The house to myself  ❤️ No nappy changes all day My personal favourite 👉 2400 margs and no hangover 🍸 Truth is... We are burnt out AF as mothers in 2026. These aren’t ‘treats’, they are basic human needs of rest, appreciation and alone time. P.S. To the brands follow